  "decision": "Held the $5K estimate at 62% and the $10K estimate at 30%. Four consecutive finalized ETF inflow sessions added $602.8M, staking rose to 43.53M ETH, and daily L1 fees and revenue improved materially, strengthening institutional demand and the nearer-term value-capture score. The Federal Reserve's proposed GENIUS Act rules provide a clearer path for regulated stablecoin issuers, but remain proposed and blockchain-neutral. ETH stayed near $2.68K, while negative bridge flows and the much larger application-fee pool limited the upgrade. Restrictive global rates remain the main cyclical headwind and are assessed separately from the unchanged structural fiscal-debasement thesis. The evidence improves weighted signals without resolving the explicit ETH value-capture hurdle for $10K, so neither probability changes. No catalyst crossed a color threshold and no thesis-breaking event occurred."
